{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbmAum959MWx6tqosATK", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags in this project are simple and file-based. I checked this against the code, and it matches the project's stored convention.\n\n**How it works**\n- `flags.toml` at the repo root lists every flag under a `[flags]` table. Names are kebab-case. Right now it has one flag:\n  ```toml\n  [flags]\n  invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n  ```\n- `src/flags.py` reads that file once at import time. It provides `is_on(name)`, which returns a bool, and `all_flags()`.\n- The convention is to read flags only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")`, not by parsing the TOML yourself.\n\n**For your checkout flow**\n1. Declare the flag in `flags.toml`, off by default:\n   ```toml\n   [flags]\n   invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n   new-checkout-flow = false\n   ```\n2. Gate the code:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags  # match however flags is imported where you use it\n\n   if flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\"):\n       return new_checkout(...)\n   return legacy_checkout(...)\n   ```\n\n**Things to watch for**\n- **A typo silently returns False.** `is_on` uses `_FLAGS.get(name, False)`, so a misspelled or undeclared name just reads as off, with no error. Copy the flag name exactly from `flags.toml`.\n- **Changes need a restart.** Flags load once at import, so editing `flags.toml` won't affect a running process.\n- **No per-user or percentage rollout.** Each flag is a single global on/off value. If you need to roll the checkout out gradually, `flags.py` would need extending.\n\nWant me to add the flag and wire it into the checkout code?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 428, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24781, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 428}, "output_tokens": 8, "ser